.SH "NAME"
pcre2_code_copy_with_tables \- copy a compiled pattern and its character tables
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.nf
.fam C
#include <pcre2.h>

pcre2_code *pcre2_code_copy_with_tables(const pcre2_code *code);
.fam
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
This function makes a copy of the memory used for a compiled pattern, excluding
any memory used by the JIT compiler. Without a subsequent call to
\f(CRpcre2_jit_compile()\fP, the copy can be used only for non\-JIT matching.
Unlike \f(CRpcre2_code_copy()\fP, a separate copy of the character tables is also
made, with the new code pointing to it. This memory will be automatically freed
when \f(CRpcre2_code_free()\fP is called. The yield of the function is NULL if
\fIcode\fP is NULL or if sufficient memory cannot be obtained.
.sp
There is a complete description of the PCRE2 native API in the
\f(CRpcre2api\fP
page and a description of the POSIX API in the
\f(CRpcre2posix\fP
page.